athogenic variants') and the Results wording ('mutations') are cohort-level statements that do not name a group of one value for these persons and give no per-person value (v5, D-29). (2) Ages: the only per-person age is 'Age at VCE' per procedure, so age_at_last_evaluation_original_text records the age printed for that patient's last VCE (Patient 2 = 10, Patient 5 = 7, Patient 9 = 6, Patient 12 = 9, Patient 32 = 13); Patient 9's second VCE row has no age printed, so the age of the first (6) is used. Age at onset is not stated per person (the Introduction's 'onset before 6 years of age' is the VEOIBD definition, not a patient fact), so it is 'not reported'. (3) ethnicity_or_country is 'not reported' because only the study's country (China) is stated, not any patient's ancestry or country. (4) 'normal' cells in Table S1 describe a whole examined segment; under D-27 they name no specific abnormality to rule out, so no 'excluded' rows were emitted and no checklist item is 'excluded'. 'not performed' and blank cells were treated as not reported. (5) The group sentence 'All patients with TNFAIP3 mutations except one suffered from ileal ulcers' does not name which patient was the exception, so it was not used to exclude anything; per-patient observed features come from each patient's own Table S1 rows. (6) '4 (10.8%) patients had recurrent infections' gives no names, so no individual was marked for recurrent infections. (7) Contradiction/inconsistency inside the paper: monogenic IBD is '18 patients (48.6%)' in Results but '45% of patients had monogenic IBD' in the Discussion, and Table 1 totals 55 procedures while the text states 58 VCE procedures. (8) is_proband is false (the paper never calls any of these patients a proband or index case) and cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is false (the paper nowhere states that any of its patients were published earlier); neither has a quotable span, so both have span null. (9) HPO candidates are left null because I was not certai